        <div class="row">
            
       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Rajya Shiksha Kendra result name wise 2026">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">Rajya Shiksha Kendra (RSKMP) Class 5th &amp; 8th Results 2026 Declared: Your Guide to Checking Scores Name-Wise and More!</h1>
                    <p class="lead">The wait is finally over for millions of students across Madhya Pradesh! The Rajya Shiksha Kendra (RSKMP) has officially announced the Class 5th and 8th annual examination results for 2026. The results were declared on March 25, 2026, at 1:30 PM, bringing excitement and anticipation to students, parents, and educators alike. This year, the overall pass percentage has seen a positive increase, with girls outperforming boys in both classes, showcasing commendable academic achievements across the state.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Check Your RSKMP Class 5th &amp; 8th Results 2026</h2>
                    <p>Accessing your RSKMP Class 5th and 8th results is a straightforward process. Students can easily check their scorecards online using their Roll Number or Samagra ID. Here’s a detailed guide to help you retrieve your results:</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Website</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the official website of Rajya Shiksha Kendra at <a href="https://rskmp.in" target="_blank">rskmp.in</a>. You might also find direct links on affiliated portals like mpresults.nic.in or mpbse.nic.in.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for a prominent link such as "View Class 5th &amp; 8th Result 2025-26" or "MP Board 5th Result 2026" / "MP Board 8th Result 2026." Click on the relevant link.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Login Credentials</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You will be prompted to enter your login details. Students typically need to provide their Roll Number or Samagra ID. Ensure these details are entered accurately.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Complete the Captcha (if required)</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Some portals may require you to enter a captcha code for verification.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">5. Submit and View Result</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Click on the "Submit" or "Show Result" button. Your RSKMP Class 5th or 8th result will then be displayed on the screen, showing subject-wise marks, total scores, and your qualifying status.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">6. Download and Print</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">It is highly recommended to download the provisional marksheet PDF and take a printout for your records. This provisional document will serve as immediate proof of your performance until the official marksheets are distributed by your respective schools.</div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="highlight-text"><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Keep your Roll Number and Samagra ID handy before the results are announced to ensure a smooth and quick checking process. In some cases, schools and teachers can also view student-wise results for their respective institutions.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Key Highlights and Performance Statistics for RSKMP 2026 Results</h2>
                    <p>The 2026 RSKMP Class 5th and 8th results reflect a commendable performance from the students. Here's a snapshot of the key statistics:</p>

                    <div class="benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Overall Pass Percentage:</strong> The pass percentage has increased by approximately 3% this year compared to previous years.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Girls Outshine Boys:</strong> Girls have achieved a higher success rate in both Class 5 and Class 8.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Over 23 Lakh Students Participated:</strong> Approximately 12 lakh students appeared for Class 5th exams and around 11 lakh for Class 8th exams.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h3 class="section-title">Detailed Pass Percentage Breakdown</h3>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Class</th>
                                <th>Overall Pass Percentage 2026</th>
                                <th>Girls Pass Percentage 2026</th>
                                <th>Boys Pass Percentage 2026</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Class 5th</td>
                                <td>95.14%</td>
                                <td>96.19%</td>
                                <td>94.15%</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Class 8th</td>
                                <td>93.83%</td>
                                <td>94.98%</td>
                                <td>92.74%</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p>These figures highlight the dedication and hard work of both students and educators in Madhya Pradesh.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Important Dates to Remember</h2>
                    <div class="benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Class 5 Exams:</strong> February 20 to February 26, 2026</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Class 8 Exams:</strong> February 20 to February 28, 2026</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Result Declaration Date:</strong> March 25, 2026</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Result Declared Time:</strong> 01:30 PM</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Official Marksheet Distribution:</strong> Expected by April 2026 through respective schools.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Understanding Your Provisional Marksheet</h2>
                    <p>The online provisional marksheet provides crucial information about your performance. It typically includes the following details:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Student's Name and Roll Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Parent's Name</p>
                        <p>✅ School Name</p>
                        <p>✅ Subject-wise Marks</p>
                        <p>✅ Total Marks and Percentage</p>
                        <p>✅ Grade</p>
                        <p>✅ Qualifying Status (Pass/Fail)</p>
                    </div>
                    <p>Students are advised to carefully review all the details mentioned in their provisional scorecard. In case of any discrepancies, it is important to contact your school authorities immediately.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">What if You Didn't Qualify?</h2>
                    <p>For students who may not have achieved the required passing marks, it's important to remember that this is not the end. To qualify for the Class 5 and 8 board exams, students must secure at least 33% marks in each subject and overall. If a student fails in one or two subjects, they will typically have the opportunity to appear for compartment exams. However, those who fail in more than two subjects may be required to repeat the entire academic session. Details regarding re-exam dates will be announced by the board at a later stage.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Conclusion</h2>
                    <p>The declaration of the Rajya Shiksha Kendra Class 5th and 8th results for 2026 marks a significant milestone in the academic journey of countless students. Congratulations to all who have successfully cleared their examinations! For those who need to improve their scores, remember that perseverance and hard work always pay off. Stay tuned to the official RSKMP website for any further updates regarding mark sheet distribution and supplementary examinations.</p>
                </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
